note The arrow at the left of a step header collapses the steps under it: they disappear from the document and the header shows how many are hidden (+n). The reader reaches for it to skip a branch already understood, or skim structure, instead of scrolling past every nested step. Pressed again it expands them. Only a step with children has the arrow. Selecting a step inside a collapsed subtree expands it.

